<title>RUSSIA: Russia non-CIS Jan-Feb aluminium, nickel exports up.</title>
<headline>Russia non-CIS Jan-Feb aluminium, nickel exports up.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian primary aluminium exports outside the Commonwealth of Independent States rose four percent year-on-year to 417,300 tonnes in January-February, the State Statistics Committee said on Monday.</p>
<p>The committee, quoted by Interfax news agency, also said non-CIS nickel exports jumped 20 percent to 27,900 tonnes from 23,200 tonnes in the same year-ago period.  </p>
<p>Non-CIS copper exports rose eight percent to 88,100 tonnes in January-February from 81,300 tonnes in the previous year's period.</p>
<p>The committee gave the following data --</p>
<p>RUSSIAN NON-CIS JAN-FEB METAL EXPORTS (THOUSAND TONNES)</p>
<p>			    Jan-Feb 1997	 Jan-Feb 1996</p>
<p>Primary aluminium	  417.3		  401.2</p>
<p>Nickel			  27.9		   23.2</p>
<p>Copper			  88.1		   81.3</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom +7095 941 8520</p>
